cant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KYOWA HAKKO KOGYO CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMODA, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASHIKAWA NOBUHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO KUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO YASUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMODA YUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASHIKAWA, NOBUHITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, KUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, YASUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMODA, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method of stabilizing an aqueous solution containing either a pyrazoloacridone derivative represented by general formula (I), {wherein R&lt;1a&gt;, R&lt;1b&gt;, R&lt;1c&gt;, and R&lt;1d&gt; each represents hydrogen, lower alkyl, -(CH2)p-X (wherein X represents hydroxy, lower alkoxy, or -NR&lt;2a&gt;R&lt;2b&gt;), or -CH((CH2)nOH)2} or a pharmacologically acceptable salt thereof, characterized by adding an acid to the aqueous solution, replacing the air present in a closed container containing the aqueous solution with an inert gas, and sealing the container.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de stabilisation d'une solution aqueuse contenant, soit un dérivé pyrazoloacridone représenté par la formule générale (I), {dans laquelle R&lt;1a&gt;, R&lt;1b&gt;, R&lt;1c&gt; et R&lt;1d&gt; représentant chacun hydrogène, alkyle inférieur, -(CH2)p-X (X représentant hydroxy, alcoxy inférieur, ou -NR&lt;2a&gt;R&lt;2b&gt;), ou -CH((CH2)nOH)2}, soit un sel de celui-ci, acceptable au plan pharmacologique. Ledit procédé consiste à ajouter un acide à la solution aqueuse, à remplacer par un gaz inerte l'air présent dans un récipient fermé contenant la solution aqueuse et à fermer le récipient hermétiquement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>